Build instructions

Save as tinyunlock.c and run:

gcc -O2 -s -o tinyunlock tinyunlock.c


(distribute the binary tinyunlock to players)




What to look for (hints)

Run strings tinyunlock — look for short ASCII data.

Use objdump -d or open in Ghidra / IDA to find the encoded array and the loop.

The transform is very simple: each input character is added by 2 before comparison.


  

Progressive hints (give one at a time)

(Hint 1) There’s a tiny static byte array inside the binary — that’s the encoded key.

(Hint 2) The check does t = s[i] + 2; compare t to encoded[i].

(Hint 3) Reverse: orig = encoded[i] - 2.
